            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to be baffled, then the Marathi for to be amazed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: समाधान",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "समाधान — samādhān — \"satisfaction; contentment\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "काम पूर्ण झाल्यावर त्याला समाधान वाटलं. kām pūrṇa jhālyāvar tyālā samādhān vāṭlaṁ. He felt satisfied when the work was done."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "समाधान (samādhān) वाटणे, with the dative; समाधानी, content."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "समाधान (samādhān) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit samādhāna, \"putting together; reconciliation\" (CDIAL 13210); in Marathi it is contentment."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
